 "name": "cfg-language",
 "title": "The language of S → aSc | b",
 "body": "<style>\n#fig text.tex, #fig text.tex-i { font-size: 11px; }\n@media (max-width: 600px) { #fig text.tex, #fig text.tex-i { font-size: 17px; } }\n</style>\n<header class=\"head\">\n  <p class=\"tag\">[practice question from your notes, answer checked]</p>\n  <h1 class=\"question\">Describe in set notation the language of \\(S \\to aSc \\mid b\\).</h1>\n</header>\n<div class=\"board work-first\">\n  <div class=\"work\">\n    <div class=\"step\" data-step=\"1\">\n      <div class=\"n\">1</div>\n      <p><span class=\"runin\">Base case:</span> the rule \\(S \\to b\\) ends every derivation and puts one \\(b\\) in the middle: \\(S \\Rightarrow b\\).</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"step\" data-step=\"2\">\n      <div class=\"n\">2</div>\n      <div class=\"body\">\n        <p><span class=\"runin\">Recursive rule:</span> each use of \\(S \\to aSc\\) adds one \\(a\\) on the left and one \\(c\\) on the right, around the \\(S\\) that is still to be replaced:</p>\n        <p>\\[ S \\Rightarrow aSc \\Rightarrow aaScc \\Rightarrow aabcc \\]</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"step\" data-step=\"3\">\n      <div class=\"n\">3</div>\n      <div class=\"body\">\n        <p><span class=\"runin\">Count:</span> applying \\(S \\to aSc\\) \\(n\\) times, for any \\(n \\ge 0\\), and then \\(S \\to b\\) once gives</p>\n        <p>\\[ S \\Rightarrow^{*} a^{n}Sc^{n} \\Rightarrow a^{n}bc^{n} \\]</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"step\" data-step=\"4\">\n      <div class=\"n\">4</div>\n      <div class=\"body\">\n        <p><span class=\"runin\">The shortest strings:</span></p>\n        <div class=\"table-wrap\">\n          <table>\n            <tr><th scope=\"col\">\\(n\\)</th><th scope=\"col\">0</th><th scope=\"col\">1</th><th scope=\"col\" data-highlight=\"4\">2</th><th scope=\"col\">3</th></tr>\n            <tr><th scope=\"row\">string</th><td><span class=\"sym\">b</span></td><td><span class=\"sym\">abc</span></td><td data-highlight=\"4\"><span class=\"sym\">aabcc</span></td><td><span class=\"sym\">aaabccc</span></td></tr>\n          </table>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"step\" data-step=\"5\">\n      <div class=\"n\">5</div>\n      <div class=\"body\">\n        <p>The parse tree of <span class=\"sym\">aabcc</span> (\\(n = 2\\)): reading its leaves from left to right gives <span class=\"sym\">aabcc</span>.</p>\n        <p class=\"answer\">\\(L = \\{a^{n}bc^{n} \\mid n \\ge 0\\}\\)</p>\n        <p>As the course conventions ask, the range of \\(n\\) is stated.</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <figure>\n    <svg id=\"fig\" viewBox=\"0 0 360 255\" role=\"img\">\n      <title>Parse tree of aabcc</title>\n      <desc>The root S has the children a, S and c, left to right. That S has the children a, S and c. That S has the one child b. Reading the leaves from left to right gives aabcc.</desc>\n      <g data-step=\"5\">\n        <line class=\"ink\" x1=\"168.2\" y1=\"35.5\" x2=\"51.8\" y2=\"89.5\" pathLength=\"1\"/>\n        <line class=\"ink\" x1=\"180\" y1=\"43\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"82\" pathLength=\"1\"/>\n        <line class=\"ink\" x1=\"191.8\" y1=\"35.5\" x2=\"308.2\" y2=\"89.5\" pathLength=\"1\"/>\n        <line class=\"ink\" x1=\"170.5\" y1=\"103.8\" x2=\"119.5\" y2=\"151.2\" pathLength=\"1\"/>\n        <line class=\"ink\" x1=\"180\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"147\" pathLength=\"1\"/>\n        <line class=\"ink\" x1=\"189.5\" y1=\"103.8\" x2=\"240.5\" y2=\"151.2\" pathLength=\"1\"/>\n        <line class=\"ink\" x1=\"180\" y1=\"173\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"212\" pathLength=\"1\"/>\n        <text class=\"tex-i\" x=\"180\" y=\"35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">S</text>\n        <text class=\"tex\" x=\"40\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a</text>\n        <text class=\"tex-i\" x=\"180\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\">S</text>\n        <text class=\"tex\" x=\"320\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\">c</text>\n        <text class=\"tex\" x=\"110\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a</text>\n      